WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:00.990
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Are you building

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:02.880
conversational
experience but would

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.240
like to cut down your
design and deployment time?

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.240
Stick around as I show
you the pre-built agent

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.845
templates in Dialogflow CX.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:18.700
Hi.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.080
I'm Priyanka Vergadia.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.780
In this episode of
Deconstructing Chatbots,

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.080
I'm going to show you how
to decrease your design

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.790
time by using Dialogflow CX
pre-built agent template.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.430
Although we are not
traveling like we used to,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.700
we may be renting cars
to get around safely.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.690
Let's see how our friends at
AlphaCar, a rental company,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.170
can easily deploy
a booking agent.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.870
Imagine you are a
manager at AlphaCar

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.220
and have noticed an uptick
in chatbot and email volume.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.190
But you have a small number
of customer service agents

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:57.340
and not a lot of experience
deploying a chat agent.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.420
That is a perfect scenario for
a pre-built agent template.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.540
Let's see how to set
it up in the console.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.720
The first step will be to
create a Google Cloud platform

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.400
account and a project.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.490
If you already have one,
don't worry about this step.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.230
Then go to the
Dialogflow CX console.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.380
Click on the project
we just created

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.450
to import the pre-built agent.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:22.030
And click Use Pre-Built Agents.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.720
We see a number of templated
agents that we can import.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:30.340
For AlphaCar, let's import
the travel car rental agent.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.640
Select a desired
location, and create.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.390
We now have the foundational
architecture for our agent.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.250
Let's see how the agent
currently functions.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.630
Best way to do that is to
navigate to the Test Agent

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.910
button and start a conversation.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.790
Now that we know how
it currently works,

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.430
let's modify some of
the agent's responses

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.670
to make it customized
to AlphaCar, starting

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.780
with the default welcome intent
response on the Start page.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.440
While we are here, let's also
modify the sign-off messages

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.250
at the end.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.130
Now let's take a look
at our custom entities.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.740
Perhaps AlphaCar only
offers a select few cars.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.670
So let's swap out the
Mitsubishi Mirage and Nissan

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.810
Versa with Ford Fusion
and Chevy Malibu.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.650
We will add some synonyms
and name variations, too.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.480
Now that we've changed
these custom entities,

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.620
let's change the agent
option that are provided

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.400
in the middle of the flow.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.310
We are going to click
on the Mitsubishi

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.590
Mirage and the
Nissan Versa pages

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.710
and change the necessary
information in the entry

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.460
dialog.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.920
In production,
these page options

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.230
may be fed by
dynamic integrations

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.810
with an inventory CRM, but
for the purpose of this demo,

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:57.880
we will hardcode these options.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.770
Now we have a customized
flow for AlphaCar.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:05.340
Let's say AlphaCar knows they
get a number of questions

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.440
about forms of
payment, and they want

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.990
to be able to answer those
to contain their users.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:14.700
Let's create a route group with
a couple of common questions,

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.820
like what forms of
payment do you accept,

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.760
and when will my
account be debited.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.120
To do that, we will go
to create a route group.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.720
We will name it Payment
Questions and add Route.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.440
Then we will create an intent
for each of those questions

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.540
with some training phrases.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.870
Once we have added these
training phrases and the route,

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:37.920
we save them.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.690
We can enter the fulfillment
response now, as well.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.800
For instance, we accept
Visa, American Express,

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.230
and Mastercard, and
your account will

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.200
be debited when you
return your car rental.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.980
Now let's add that route
group to the Car Option page

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.300
under Add Route Type
inside Route Groups.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:57.960
Great.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.050
Now let's test the agent
using the simulator

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.660
to make sure everything's
working as expected.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:11.910
Yay, everything seems to be
triggering appropriately.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:14.990
Now let's add this
flow as a test case.

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:18.800
Test cases allow us to uncover
bugs and prevent regression.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.769
We can then revisit
this flow and others

00:04:21.769 --> 00:04:25.820
in the Test Case section, which
allows us to rerun all the test

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.420
cases, import and export,
and view the test coverage

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.300
for transitions and intents.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.030
This will help us make
sure we're testing

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.020
every part of the agent.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.100
It's also a good idea to look
at the validation section

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.730
to see if there are any
recommendations or errors.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.940
It seems like it has spotted
similar training phrases

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.950
across multiple intents.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:52.260
This can present NLU
confusion down the line,

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:56.150
so best to resolve that
by deleting or modifying

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.920
selected training phrases.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.530
Let's fast forward to
being ready to deploy.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.390
We're going to want
to use versions

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:06.020
to move our current development
environment into production.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:09.235
A draft flow is updated every
time a developer on our team

00:05:09.235 --> 00:05:10.640
makes a change.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:14.060
As a best practice, we should
always test our draft flows

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.580
before promoting them
to production versions,

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.400
although we can always roll
back to previous versions

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.740
if any problems are discovered.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:26.120
With that, our AlphaCar
agent is now live.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.610
All that's left to
do is to regularly

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.920
look at the analytics
section to improve

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:34.890
the agent by assessing how
it's being used in production.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:38.210
All right, so we just created
an entire conversational

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:42.350
experience to book a rental
car in literally five minutes.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:45.350
That's exactly what pre-built
agent templates are for.

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:48.080
They increase the
speed to market.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.550
Now it's your turn.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:52.880
Explore a pre-built agent that
makes sense for your project

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:56.210
and share your experience
with me in the comments below.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:59.860
[MUSIC PLAYING]

